        <!--
          Publish a release with ./Scripts/release.sh (see RELEASING.md) — in practice via
          `./release-on-airy.sh PurpleMonitor` from the repo root, since releases are cut on
          the runner. It builds + notarizes + zips the app, EdDSA-signs the zip, creates a
          tagged GitHub release on the PUBLIC bronty13/phantomlives-releases repo, prepends a
          new <item> here, and mirrors this file to that public repo.

          Sparkle reads the MIRRORED copy via raw.githubusercontent.com. This file is the
          source of truth; the public repo holds the served copy. The feed must never point
          at the private monorepo — anonymous clients 404 and can never update again.

          DO NOT hand-edit a shipped <item>: its version + EdDSA signature pair is part of
          the trust chain. Add new items above older ones.

          (No <item> yet — this item-less channel is the bootstrap. It exists so the very
          first release's feed-reachability guard has a real 200 to fetch; release.sh adds
          the first real item.)
        -->
